# Line-ending contract. Without this, core.autocrlf=true checks out committed
# .sh files with CRLF and bash dies on `$'\r'` — a failure that reads as a
# script bug, not a checkout bug. (Cross-repo handoff, 2026-07-30.)
#
# NOTE: scripts/spark_wsl.ps1 ALSO base64-encodes bash across the shell
# boundary. That is deliberately kept — it defends against PowerShell/bash
# QUOTING as well as line endings, and quoting bit us twice while building it.
# This file makes committed shell scripts safe; the base64 hop makes inline
# scripts safe. Different problems.

*.sh    text eol=lf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.ipynb text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text
*.parquet binary
*.mp3     binary
*.png     binary
